1
00:00:00,720 --> 00:00:03,140
Hello everyone and welcome to EnglishPod.

2
00:00:03,360 --> 00:00:04,360
My name is Marco.

3
00:00:04,360 --> 00:00:08,340
My name is Catherine and today we're talking about someone who's very, very dirty.

4
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:15,520
That's right and actually not only are we talking about something being dirty but also that we want to clean everything.

5
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:20,100
Okay, so you'll learn how to call someone who likes clean things in English today.

6
00:00:20,580 --> 00:00:21,840
Let's take a listen to our dialogue.

7
00:00:27,520 --> 00:00:28,700
This bathroom is a pigsty.

8
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:32,160
Helen, why do you keep flushing the toilet?

9
00:00:32,260 --> 00:00:32,700
What's wrong?

10
00:00:33,140 --> 00:00:34,260
I just can't stand it.

11
00:00:34,420 --> 00:00:35,400
It's really gross in here.

12
00:00:35,860 --> 00:00:39,780
There's a stain on the toilet seat and the floor was wet and slippery so I cleaned it.

13
00:00:40,300 --> 00:00:41,060
You did what?

14
00:00:41,580 --> 00:00:45,540
Helen, I know it's gross but I've seen many public washrooms that are much worse.

15
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:48,180
Why are you cleaning the countertop?

16
00:00:48,760 --> 00:00:49,740
Are you out of your mind?

17
00:00:50,580 --> 00:00:51,260
I can't help myself.

18
00:00:51,540 --> 00:00:52,980
It's just so disgusting in here.

19
00:00:53,440 --> 00:00:55,580
Helen, this is not like your own bathroom.

20
00:00:56,420 --> 00:00:57,640
Just leave it to the cleaners, okay?

21
00:00:58,160 --> 00:01:00,960
Hang on, I'm just going to quickly wipe the sink and sweep the floor.

22
00:01:00,960 --> 00:01:02,360
You're such a neat freak.

23
00:01:02,800 --> 00:01:03,320
I'm out of here.

24
00:01:11,510 --> 00:01:12,350
Alright we're back.

25
00:01:12,840 --> 00:01:17,810
So this girl was very much of a neat freak and we're going to take a look at that word a little bit later on.

26
00:01:18,360 --> 00:01:22,190
Why don't we go back to the very beginning and take a look at some vocab on Language Takeaway.

27
00:01:25,120 --> 00:01:25,720
Language Takeaway

28
00:01:28,400 --> 00:01:32,140
The first word we have here on Language Takeaway today is pigsty.

29
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:35,220
This bathroom is a pigsty.

30
00:01:35,880 --> 00:01:39,480
Okay, so pigsty is a place where pigs live.

31
00:01:41,400 --> 00:01:49,480
Now this obviously, the bathroom is not really a place where pigs live so if you call something a pigsty, you're saying that it's very dirty.

32
00:01:49,480 --> 00:01:50,300
You're saying it's disgusting.

33
00:01:50,960 --> 00:01:53,380
It's very, very dirty like a pigsty.

34
00:01:53,840 --> 00:01:58,440
So actually if you go to a farm and you see where all the pigs are, that is actually called a pigsty.

35
00:01:58,920 --> 00:02:01,920
Right, there's mud and dirt and yeah, that's a pigsty.

36
00:02:02,200 --> 00:02:05,200
So someone who is very, very dirty, you can also call a pig.

37
00:02:05,620 --> 00:02:12,380
Okay, now she was saying that the bathroom is so dirty and it's really gross in here.

38
00:02:12,720 --> 00:02:17,670
Okay, so gross means something is, she doesn't like it.

39
00:02:17,880 --> 00:02:21,240
It's really dirty and you know, makes her uncomfortable.

40
00:02:21,240 --> 00:02:25,990
So something that doesn't taste good, you can say it's gross.

41
00:02:26,920 --> 00:02:27,920
That's right.

42
00:02:27,920 --> 00:02:28,490
So I don't like to eat snake.

43
00:02:28,920 --> 00:02:30,370
I think eating snake is gross.

44
00:02:30,840 --> 00:02:32,150
Okay, very good.

45
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:40,270
So something that is gross is something that's not really nice, maybe it tastes bad or it smells bad, something that is bad in general.

46
00:02:40,450 --> 00:02:40,750
That's right.

47
00:02:41,150 --> 00:02:47,530
Okay, so she went on to talk about the toilet seat and that there was a stain on the toilet seat.

48
00:02:47,830 --> 00:02:50,070
Okay, a stain is usually a bad thing.

49
00:02:50,370 --> 00:02:57,250
It means that there's a color or a mark that's permanent or maybe can be washed away on something.

50
00:02:57,550 --> 00:03:00,590
So in this case, the toilet seat has a mark on it.

51
00:03:01,480 --> 00:03:10,320
Maybe it's brown or yellow, but I can also say, I was drinking wine and I spilled the wine on my shirt and it left a stain.

52
00:03:10,320 --> 00:03:14,520
So now there's always this red part on my shirt.

53
00:03:14,520 --> 00:03:15,050
It won't go away.

54
00:03:15,520 --> 00:03:19,230
Okay, so a stain is a mark that usually won't go away.

55
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:24,030
So then she went on to describe the bathroom as being disgusting.

56
00:03:24,480 --> 00:03:26,520
So I guess this is very similar to gross.

57
00:03:26,520 --> 00:03:26,670
That's right.

58
00:03:27,520 --> 00:03:29,330
Something that is gross is usually also disgusting.

59
00:03:29,990 --> 00:03:32,210
I can say, oh, this food is awful.

60
00:03:32,510 --> 00:03:33,730
It's just disgusting.

61
00:03:34,790 --> 00:03:38,260
But I can also say in this case, oh, your room is disgusting.

62
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:39,620
You need to clean it.

63
00:03:39,760 --> 00:03:42,560
It's so dirty or bad or unappealing.

64
00:03:42,860 --> 00:03:46,980
So something that is gross, something that is disgusting is something negative.

65
00:03:49,240 --> 00:03:54,600
And then we have our keyword and the title of this lesson for today, a neat freak.

66
00:03:55,160 --> 00:03:57,000
Her friend says, you're such a neat freak.

67
00:03:57,400 --> 00:03:57,920
That's right.

68
00:03:58,180 --> 00:04:02,220
So a neat freak is someone who likes things to be very clean.

69
00:04:03,780 --> 00:04:07,150
And so a neat freak does not live in a pigsty.

70
00:04:07,920 --> 00:04:10,480
A neat freak does not like to be in pigsties.

71
00:04:10,480 --> 00:04:15,360
A neat freak likes things to be in order and organized and clean.

72
00:04:15,360 --> 00:04:23,110
So maybe somebody that's cleaning all the time or that's very, very organized, you can say that that person is a neat freak.

73
00:04:23,560 --> 00:04:25,870
He is a neat freak or she is a neat freak.

74
00:04:26,160 --> 00:04:31,210
Now it's not necessarily a good thing to be a neat freak, but it's not terrible either to call somebody a neat freak.

75
00:04:31,570 --> 00:04:33,310
You can say, hey, are you a neat freak?

76
00:04:33,820 --> 00:04:34,160
Right.

77
00:04:34,680 --> 00:04:37,440
That means, are you really concerned about cleanliness?

78
00:04:37,440 --> 00:04:38,440
Uh-huh.

79
00:04:38,440 --> 00:04:39,440
OK.

80
00:04:39,440 --> 00:04:40,440
Very good.

81
