00:05:37,020 --> 00:05:37,760
Fluency Builder.

105
00:05:38,570 --> 00:05:43,410
So the first thing we want to talk about today is this phrase, I can't stand it.

106
00:05:43,760 --> 00:05:45,170
So this is our neat freak talking.

107
00:05:45,600 --> 00:05:48,150
She says, I just can't stand it.

108
00:05:48,510 --> 00:05:49,990
I just can't stand it.

109
00:05:50,110 --> 00:05:54,830
So if you can't stand something, that means that you can't tolerate it.

110
00:05:55,350 --> 00:05:55,750
That's right.

111
00:05:56,600 --> 00:05:57,600
It means I don't like it.

112
00:05:57,600 --> 00:05:58,370
I don't want it anymore.

113
00:05:58,730 --> 00:05:59,670
I need to change it.

114
00:06:00,560 --> 00:06:01,560
OK.

115
00:06:01,560 --> 00:06:06,760
So for example, if a bar is too loud, you say, I have to leave.

116
00:06:06,880 --> 00:06:07,900
I can't stand it.

117
00:06:08,040 --> 00:06:09,100
It's too loud in there.

118
00:06:09,280 --> 00:06:09,720
That's right.

119
00:06:09,960 --> 00:06:15,700
Or if you are next to me all day and you do tap, tap, tap, tap, tap with your pen, I say, Marco, stop it.

120
00:06:15,860 --> 00:06:17,180
I can't stand it anymore.

121
00:06:17,680 --> 00:06:19,560
OK, very good.

122
00:06:19,560 --> 00:06:25,660
And then she went on to explain or to justify why she was cleaning the public restroom.

123
00:06:26,320 --> 00:06:28,080
And she said, I can't help myself.

124
00:06:28,080 --> 00:06:29,320
It's just too disgusting in here.

125
00:06:29,690 --> 00:06:30,750
I can't help myself.

126
00:06:31,130 --> 00:06:33,890
So this means that I cannot control my actions.

127
00:06:34,120 --> 00:06:36,880
OK, I cannot control what I do.

128
00:06:36,880 --> 00:06:41,630
And so in some cases, like with a neat freak, the person really needs everything to be clean.

129
00:06:42,400 --> 00:06:44,350
And so she says, I can't help myself.

130
00:06:44,650 --> 00:06:45,430
I have to clean.

131
00:06:45,920 --> 00:06:48,200
OK, so it's a phrase like this.

132
00:06:49,730 --> 00:06:54,070
Don't try to separate it and try to define what help and help yourself.

133
00:06:54,610 --> 00:06:57,880
It's more of a phrase saying, I can't control myself.

134
00:06:58,040 --> 00:06:59,600
I can't control my actions.

135
00:06:59,640 --> 00:07:00,260
I can't help myself.

136
00:07:00,740 --> 00:07:04,600
Or in the case of another person, you say, she can't help herself.

137
00:07:05,680 --> 00:07:07,040
She can't help himself.

138
00:07:07,440 --> 00:07:09,240
Right, so maybe you'd like to smoke.

139
00:07:09,240 --> 00:07:11,420
And you're smoking all the time.

140
00:07:11,520 --> 00:07:12,520
And you say, stop smoking.

141
00:07:12,540 --> 00:07:13,700
You say, I can't help myself.

142
00:07:13,920 --> 00:07:14,460
I have to smoke.

143
00:07:14,880 --> 00:07:15,880
Yeah, I have to smoke.

144
00:07:15,880 --> 00:07:19,140
OK, and for our last phrase, she said, hang on.

145
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:22,840
I'm just going to quickly wipe the sink and sweep the floor.

146
00:07:23,320 --> 00:07:23,540
Hang on.

147
00:07:24,320 --> 00:07:25,160
This means wait.

148
00:07:25,320 --> 00:07:26,320
Wait a moment.

149
00:07:26,320 --> 00:07:27,320
Yeah.

150
00:07:27,320 --> 00:07:30,000
Yeah, so this is a really common phrase we hear in English.

151
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:35,500
It's something that you'll hear all the time in a pretty relaxed environment, not maybe in school.

152
00:07:36,080 --> 00:07:38,840
But if someone says, OK, I'm going to go.

153
00:07:38,840 --> 00:07:39,180
See you later.

154
00:07:39,840 --> 00:07:42,700
And the other person wants to say something to you, say, hang on.

155
00:07:43,480 --> 00:07:43,620
Hang on.

156
00:07:44,480 --> 00:07:45,480
Wait a moment.

157
00:07:45,480 --> 00:07:46,480
I have to tell you this thing.

158
00:07:46,480 --> 00:07:49,300
So you wouldn't really use it with your boss or a customer.

159
00:07:49,540 --> 00:07:50,660
You wouldn't say, hang on a second.

160
00:07:50,970 --> 00:07:54,850
No, you would say that with a friend or family member, things like that.

161
00:07:54,960 --> 00:07:58,840
OK, so it's a very informal way of saying, wait a moment.

162
00:07:58,840 --> 00:07:59,170
Wait a minute.

163
00:07:59,840 --> 00:08:00,840
That's right.

164
00:08:00,840 --> 00:08:01,690
So the formal way is, please wait.

165
00:08:02,260 --> 00:08:02,450
Please wait.

166
00:08:03,260 --> 00:08:04,750
And the informal way is, hang on.

167
00:08:05,240 --> 00:08:05,430
Hang on.

168
00:08:06,240 --> 00:08:08,430
Or hang on a sec, which is hang on a second.

169
00:08:08,880 --> 00:08:09,470
All right.

170
